  "result": "Excellent! Customer statements are complete. All 212 tests pass.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **New src/statements.js** with `statement(customerId, invoices, asOf)` function:\n   - Validates customer exists (CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND error)\n   - Validates asOf is a valid date (DATE_INVALID error)\n   - Filters for invoices with:\n     - Matching customer (normalized ID)\n     - Status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' (excludes draft and paid)\n     - issueDate on or before asOf\n   - Returns `ok({ customerId, invoices, totalDue })` where:\n     - Each invoice has: `{ number, issueDate, dueDate, total, due }`\n     - `due` is calculated from `balanceDue(invoice)`\n     - `total` is from `invoiceTotals(invoice).total`\n     - Invoices sorted by issueDate ascending\n     - `totalDue` is sum of all due amounts\n2. **18 comprehensive tests** covering:\n   - Error cases: unknown customer, invalid date\n   - Date filtering (before, on, after asOf)\n   - Status filtering (only issued/partially_paid)\n   - Draft and paid invoice exclusion\n   - Due amount and totalDue calculations\n   - DueDate inclusion in statement\n   - Sorting and multi-customer filtering\n   - Customer ID normalization\n   - Multiple invoices with partial payments\n   - Cross-year statements\n\nStatements provide a complete view of a customer's outstanding invoices with all key details and totals.",
